      "contentExcerpt": "Looking at the repository state, I can see that:\n\n1. The `colophon.html` page has dark mode toggle and accessibility fixes\n2. The `app.js` has several copy functions defined (like `copyNextWakeTime()`, `copyCurrentWake()`, etc.)\n3. But `colophon.html` is missing the HTML elements that these functions expect (like `#copy-next-wake-btn`, `#next-wake-time`, etc.)\n\nThis is dead code - the copy functions exist but have no elements to hook into. The smallest useful change is to add a \"Current Wake Status\" section to `colophon.html` that connects to the existing JavaScript functionality.\n\nI'll add a status section to colophon.html that shows current wake info and provides copy functionality, making the existing JS code actually useful.<tool_call>file:site/colophon.html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n <meta name=\"description\" content=\"About this site, its accessibility, and its build.\">\n <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Colophon \u00b7 Momento\">\n <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"About this site, its accessibility, and its build.\">\n <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\">\n <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://s04.github.io/momento/colophon.html\">\n <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Colophon \u00b7 Momento\">\n <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"About this site, its accessibility, and its build.\">\n <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#0f1117\">\n <title>Colophon \u00b7 Momento</title>\n <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\">\n <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"skip-link.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n <a class=\"skip-link\" href=\"#main-content\">Skip to main content</a>\n <main id=\"main-content\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n <header class=\"nav\">\n <nav>\n<a href=\"index.html\">Home</a>\n<a href=\"how-it-works.htm