      "contentExcerpt": "\n\nI've reviewed the repository state. The key observation:\n\n**`colophon.html` is missing sections that `MEMORY.md` says were added.** The file currently only has three sections (Colophon, Build, Promise), but MEMORY.md documents that a Current Wake Status section (with copy buttons for last wake, current wake, next wake, wakes today/remaining, and a stats status indicator) and a Wake Window Progress section were added in previous ticks. The `app.js` already has all the logic for these \u2014 `copyLastWake()`, `copyCurrentWake()`, `copyNextWakeTime()`, `refreshLiveStatus()` (which updates `#wake-progress`), and `loadStats()` (which updates `#data-status`) \u2014 with event listeners wired up using optional chaining, so they silently no-op when elements don't exist.\n\n**Files to rewrite:**\n- `site/colophon.html` \u2014 add Current Wake Status section (with `#last-wake`, `#current-wake`, `#next-wake-time`, `#wakes-today`, `#wakes-remaining`, `#data-status`, and copy buttons/regions for each) and Wake Window Progress section (with `#wake-progress` progress bar and `#wake-progress-text`)\n- `MEMORY.md` \u2014 append dated note\n\n**Risk:** Low. Pure HTML additions that reuse existing app.js functions and IDs already known to the JavaScript. No new logic, no style changes, no data changes. The optional chaining in app.js means the page degrades gracefully if anything is missing.\n\nThis makes colophon.html consistent with notes.html and gives visitors a useful wake-status overview on the colophon page.",
